# Hamlib client traffic against Hamlib's simulator: PowerSDR (rigctl -m 2048, simpowersdr), recorded with
# rigctl -vvvvv, converted with hamlib2trace.py --text, written by cat_replay -v.
# Hamlib reads and sets the mode with ZZMD. rigctl reported LSB, PKTUSB, USB, CW, CW (no RTTY
# in the simulator). The simulator sends ZZMD with one digit and a 40 character IF, which is
# rejected as bad.
